{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/849457-where-will-i-find-information-and-or-guidance-on-using-true-fae","id":849457,"title":"Where will I find information and/or guidance on using \"True\" Fae?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-18T14:34:27-07:00","id":849457,"title":"Where will I find information and/or guidance on using \"True\" Fae?","content":"As I understand it, the advent of a &quot;changeling&quot; is the result of the Fae finding a way to shield themselves from an ever increasingly banal world. In exchange for this protection, they became inherently less magically inclined and powerful.<br /> <br /> I'm running a Mage game where there are pockets of consensual reality that are &quot;up for grabs&quot; so to speak--where there's a tug of war between the Trads and Techs for the hearts and minds of the sleepers and all that--thus, there are places were a distinctly mystical sensibility abounds, such that banality all around is low there, and would theoretically allow for the relatively stable existence of Fae without the need for the mortal shell.<br /> <br /> In the past I've read through both C:tD 2ed., DA: Fae, and a handful of source books--so I essentially understand how the game is played and how the systems work in both respective iterations of the game. However, my &quot;inside baseball&quot; knowledge of the game line is limited enough that I feel like I could look through source books, see what I'm looking for, but not realize that I'm looking at it.<br /> <br /> Little help? (Thank you in advance all!)<br /> <br /> <b>***(in the event that my knowledge is so limited on Fae that the very manner in which I've framed this question doesn't make sense, I would alternatively ask that someone please direct me at the heaviest hitters in the Fae gameline--the &quot;Methuselah&quot;/Arete 6-7/Rank 6 type characters for the game line--i.e., the most powerful character type/splat for which there are stats.)***</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T10:03:29-07:00","id":850168,"title":"","content":"True Fae are best thought of as ur-kithain, firstly, so you're unlikely to find stats for them in any CTD material. But there are the Lost Ones (really old fae, who may be True Fae but may not be, who have hidden away in forgotten freeholds and become immensely powerful).<br /> <br /> There is one in one of the Immortal Eyes books, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T13:04:11-07:00","id":850226,"title":"","content":"Many thanks for the info, I'll buy that book right away!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T18:42:02-07:00","id":850355,"title":"","content":"His power was enough that he raised an island from the sea, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T11:54:48-07:00","id":852520,"title":"","content":"I might get looked at funny for suggesting this, but Exalted was originally supposed to be a &quot;secret pre-pre-history&quot; of the WoD. The Fair Folk of 1e and to a lesser extent 2e were originally supposed to be the things that eventually became Changelings.<br /> <br /> So reading Exalted: The Fair Folk (1e) and Graceful Wicked Masques (2e) might give some inspiration.<br /> <br /> It's also one odd point where you might be well served in looking at Changeling: the Lost; the True Fae/Gentry of that setting capture about the right tones, I think. (Even if the rest is utterly foreign to how C:tD operates.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5